{
  "_comment": "Real context windows for locally-served models reached via openai/<name>. Without this aider falls back to its tiny default (~4k tokens) and silently drops files. Each entry's max_input_tokens is a deliberate agentic cap (effective_ctx - max_output_tokens); it is NOT the backend's own context setting. TWO backends are represented here. qwen3.8-27b-heretic-ara is served by NInfer on :8081 (the default; see modules/cae/ai/config.el): --max-context 200000 with --kv-capacity auto resolves to ~200064 int8 KV tokens, and NInfer does NOT halve the window the way Ollama does, so the whole thing is usable prompt -- 163840 + 32768 output lands just inside it, the larger output allowance covering reasoning tokens under --default-thinking-budget 16384. KV is a startup-fixed pool, so overrunning it queues or errors rather than spilling to host RAM. Every other entry is an Ollama tag on :11434, where usable prompt is only num_ctx/2 -- the qwen3.8:27b-ultra-uncensored-q5_k_m entry keeps 81920 + 16384 for that reason (num_ctx 196608 -> ~98304 real tokens) and must not be raised without re-measuring, since at that model's native 262144 the KV cache overflows 32G VRAM onto host RAM and decode collapses from ~44 to 3.4 tok/s. The two backends cannot run at once: 22.8G of NVFP4 weights plus KV leaves no room for Ollama's 21G Q5_K_M.",
